itle":"The governance regex misses some unlocked install forms","unit":"U0015"},{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"The change pins `hatchling==1.33.0`, but `uv.lock` does not record build dependencies. When `uv sync --locked --no-dev` builds the project in attestation.yml and human-approval.yml, uv still resolves hatchling's transitive dependencies (packaging, pathspec, pluggy, trove-classifiers) from PyPI at run time and executes them during the build. A new or compromised release of one of those packages would therefore still run code in the privileged base-trusted job. That is the same class of exposure GHSA-vp48-82vp-gr6c addresses. The docs acknowledge this residual risk, but the intent is to keep unlocked code out of these jobs, so whether to accept it is a policy decision.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F003","line":53,"path":"pyproject.toml","response_note":"Scope fixed by the requester: the advisory's proposed fix and the task decisions are to pin the build backend version only. Pinning hatchling's transitive build deps (e.g. [tool.uv] build-constraint-dependencies) or running the checker with --no-install-project to skip the build entirely are recorded in the PR as owner decisions. The residual is disclosed in docs/attestations-and-ci.md.","severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Choose one: pin the backend's transitive dependencies with `[tool.uv] build-constraint-dependencies` (and extend `test_build_backend_is_pinned` to check them), or install with `--no-install-project` and run the package from the checkout so no build happens. Otherwise, record that the residual risk is accepted.","title":"The build backend's own dependencies still resolve fresh inside the trusted pull_request_target jobs","unit":"U0012"}],"fingerprint":{"base_tree_sha":"725a2d01be4301c7430140c65460bee2beec119e","config_sha256":"47de23995384e97c1f2cfdaf65f0f5392e876c6a60064aa0be584ac5e453621c","configuration_supported":true,"diff_sha256":"ef4345